/// A local binding hides its value from the rest of the body with `have`.
///
/// A `let` is transparent, so conversion may read its value. A large
/// intermediate result should not unfold into every later type.
///
/// `have x = e;` binds `x` beside `let`. It elaborates to an auxiliary
/// definition whose unfolding name the body does not hold.
///
/// - see: #4570 — the opacity sketch, its rulings in the issue body

/// A bound read once and then only compared. The body checks against the
/// bound's type and never unfolds the search that produced it.
def withinBound(xs : List(Nat), x : Nat) -> Bool {
  have bound = maximum(xs);
  let slack = 2;
  x <= bound + slack
}
